<title>INDIA: INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, OIL, MEAL DOWN.</title>
<headline>INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, OIL, MEAL DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in the markets of central India in very thin trading as many markets were closed to mark the Hindu snake festival 'Nag Panchami'. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were bearish on very poor supplies at the upper price level. Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were bearish on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $264-265 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $94-95 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,225-3,250 rupese per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
